  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure to the east of the area will allow for dry weather\nto continue through Sunday. While a weak, dry cold front will\nenter on Monday, another high pressure system will return on\nTuesday, keeping the pattern dry and seasonable. This morning,\nthe main concern will be the trapped near surface moisture in\nNorthwest Ohio, which has turned into dense fog. A Dense Fog\nAdvisory is in effect until 10 AM. In Northeast Ohio and\nNorthwest Pennsylvania, temperatures will fall into the upper\n20s to mid 30s this morning and Sunday morning, allowing for a\nfrost/freeze setup. However, most of these counties are no\nlonger in the growing season and will not have headlines issued.",
